Package: vhs-gui
Version: @VERSION@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Suggests: vapoursynth
Maintainer: RyanEiri <RyanEiri@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/RyanEiri/vhs-gui
Description: VHS digitization GUI: capture, deinterlace, upscale and encode
 A desktop application for the VHS preservation pipeline: live capture
 monitoring, denoise and audio cleanup, QTGMC deinterlacing, IVTC and
 VDecimate, letterbox cropping, AI upscaling with resumable segment
 checkpoints, and viewer encodes.
 .
 This package ships the VapourSynth plugins that have no Python wheel
 (ffms2, fmtconv, miscfilters), built for this Ubuntu release. VapourSynth
 itself, its other plugins and the Real-ESRGAN upscaler are set up separately
 (see /usr/share/doc/vhs-gui/external-tools.md).
